- Verdict: **FULLY VERIFIED** — all round 1 findings have been addressed; no new issues found.

## Round 1 findings — status

### Finding 1 (medium) — outdated Terraform version example
**Status:** FIXED ✓

The doc now correctly cites 1.11.4 and explains the requirement:
> "then install the version the template pins in `.terraform-version` (`1.11.4` at this ref: `tfenv install 1.11.4`). The `infra/accounts` and `infra/networks` root modules declare `required_version = "~> 1.11.0"`, so an older release such as the `1.4.6` in the shipped doc will not run."

**Verified against:**
- `.terraform-version` contains `1.11.4`
- `infra/accounts/main.tf:36` and `infra/networks/providers.tf:8` both declare `required_version = "~>1.11.0"`

### Finding 2 (low) — `make infra-lint` scope overstated
**Status:** FIXED ✓

The doc now correctly describes the full scope:
> "`make infra-lint` runs the whole infra lint suite (markdown, shell scripts, Terraform, workflows), which expects these tools to be installed."

**Verified against:**
- `Makefile:146-147` confirms infra-lint is an aggregate target that runs markdown, shell scripts, terraform, and workflow checks
- Lines 64-66 of the doc now accurately reflect this aggregate nature

